\subsection{Thickness}
\label{sec:thick}
Thinner films have larger band gaps and deeper valence bands (Fig.~\ref{fig:thick}a), so ungated resistances rise steeply below six layers. At 4.8~eV the edge-contact resistance rises from 242~\ohmcm\ (12 layers) to $1.1\times10^5$~\ohmcm\ (3 layers). In the gated on state ($\Phi_M=5.0$~eV, $V_G=-3$~V) the edge contact improves monotonically with thickness (0.197$\to$0.135~\ohmcm\ from 3 to 12 layers). The top contact instead has an optimum near four layers: 0.53~\ohmcm, rising to 1.55~\ohmcm\ at 12 layers. Beyond that thickness the vertical access through layers with low $\mu_\perp$ outweighs the shallower barrier (Fig.~\ref{fig:thick}b). These trends are robust to the band alignment and to the assumed valence-band share of the confinement shift (Supplementary Section~\ref{S-sec:thickalign}). With the measured alignment and Pt contacts edge contacts again improve monotonically from 3 to 12 layers (oxide interlayer: 25$\to$4.5~\ohmcm), and top contacts have an optimum at five layers (interlayer, 207~\ohmcm) or six layers (direct pinning). Changing the valence-band share to 0.2 or 0.5 moves the optimum of the reference alignment between four and five layers. With the anisotropic mass ($m_\parallel=0.9~m_0$, two-band dispersion, most favourable straight paths) the ranking also depends on thickness (Supplementary Section~\ref{S-sec:thickdir}). With the interlayer, the top-contact resistance rises from 120~\ohmcm\ at four layers to $1.8\times10^4$~\ohmcm\ at 12 layers, because holes must cross more layers with a low $\mu_\perp$, while the edge-contact resistance falls from 1060~\ohmcm\ at three layers to 21~\ohmcm\ at 12. Top contacts are better only at four layers (1.8$\times$); edge contacts win at three layers (1.5$\times$) and from six layers on (2.0$\times$ at six, 22$\times$ at eight and 860$\times$ at 12 layers). With direct pinning top contacts are 12--27 times better from four to eight layers and edge contacts 12 times better at 12 layers. With normal paths the crossover with the interlayer lies between six and eight layers instead of between four and six.

